+## Download-folder fix — 6 October 2026
+
+The full Python suite passed **55 tests**. New integration checks saved a folder through the authenticated Settings API, reloaded it from disk, and downloaded the same synthetic local HTTP video concurrently twice. Both files landed directly in the selected folder with different names; an existing file was preserved. The same checks passed with a per-download override. Folder names containing spaces, Unicode and a literal percent sign worked. Browser copy responses matched the completed files, and History recorded the actual paths. Missing and unwritable folders failed without downloading to the default folder. All six existing real FFmpeg conversion tests also verified the output's immediate parent folder.
+
+Happy DOM checks passed for the displayed saved paths, escaped filenames, numbered “Save a copy” links and current/legacy history statuses. Ruff and JavaScript syntax checks passed. The update patch was applied to the previous ZIP's source and its result compared byte-for-byte with this version. Windows and full browser rendering remain unverified here.
